-- Voting Record — 117th/118th roll calls for the Phase A landmarks (data-only)
-- ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
-- GENERATED by scripts/vr-gen-phase-a-vote-migration.mjs from
-- db/vr-phase-a-vote-seed.json and db/vr-issue-seed.json — do not hand-edit;
-- regenerate from the seeds.
--
-- WHY THIS MIGRATION EXISTS
-- Migration 20260810000000 created 15 enacted landmarks from the 117th and 118th
-- Congresses and gave them 51 curated issue rows. It said plainly, in its own
-- header, that it would move the ranking by exactly zero: an issue mapping is only
-- half of a scoreable record, and the vote tables held no 117th or 118th member
-- votes to pair it with. This migration supplies the other half.
--
-- 29 roll calls (14 House, 15 Senate), 731 attributed member votes.
--
-- HOW THE ROLLS WERE CHOSEN
-- Every <recordedVote> block for all 15 measures was read out of govinfo BILLSTATUS
-- bulk data. That is a much larger set than what is here — the Inflation Reduction
-- Act alone carries 41 Senate roll calls, almost all of them vote-a-rama amendments,
-- and the American Rescue Plan carries 38. From each measure's list, ONE decisive
-- vote per chamber is taken: final passage, or the motion to concur / conference
-- report where that was the chamber's last act on the bill.
--
-- Procedural rolls are deliberately excluded. A cloture motion, a budget-point-of-
-- order waiver and a motion to table are votes about floor process; attaching an
-- issue position to one puts a receipt on a member's profile that the vote does not
-- support. This is the same reason the repo leaves "providing for consideration"
-- rule resolutions unmapped (db/vr-ingest-runbook.md, "Rules are not policy").
--
-- EVERY ROLL WAS RE-VERIFIED AGAINST THE CHAMBER'S OWN RECORD
-- The build script re-fetched each selected roll from clerk.house.gov/evs (House) or
-- senate.gov/legislative/LIS/roll_call_votes (Senate) and dropped it unless the
-- document's own bill citation matched the measure and its question was a decisive
-- one. That check earned its keep immediately: Phase A had recorded House roll
-- 120/2024 for H.R. 7888, and the Clerk's record shows roll 120 is "Table Motion to
-- Reconsider" — the passage vote is roll 119, 273-147. Roll 119 is what is ingested
-- here. Reading the source caught it; trusting the earlier note would not have.
--
-- ATTRIBUTION IS FAIL-CLOSED
-- The House XML carries a bioguide id per legislator, so the House side is a direct
-- db/vr-member-map.json lookup. The Senate XML carries no bioguide id, so senators
-- are resolved by (last name, state) against the roster and accepted only on a
-- UNIQUE hit. Every roll in the seed resolved with zero ambiguities and zero
-- unreadable positions. Unmapped members are dropped at build time, so there is no
-- name matching anywhere in this SQL.
--
-- THE ROSTER IS THE CEILING, NOT THE CHAMBER
-- db/vr-member-map.json holds 63 bioguide→slug entries, so a House roll can attribute
-- at most 38 of ~430 votes cast and a Senate roll at most 18 of 100. The per-roll
-- attributed counts below are low for that reason and no other: the totals stored on
-- each roll call are the FULL chamber tallies from the official record, and is_party
-- was computed from the full member list before filtering, so a party-crossover flag
-- is never an artifact of the subset. Widening the roster is a separate pass.
--
-- WHAT REMAINS UNSCOREABLE, AND WHY
-- H.R. 7776 (FY23 NDAA) gets its Senate roll 396 (83-11) but no House roll. The only
-- House vote on that vehicle is roll 253/2022, a suspension vote on the rivers-and-
-- harbors bill that held the number before the NDAA text replaced it; ingesting it
-- would record a defense-authorization position from a water-projects vote.
--
-- H.R. 815 gets its Senate roll 154 (79-18) but the House never voted the package at
-- all. It passed four division bills on 2024-04-20 and H.Res. 1160 folded them into
-- the Senate amendment. Only one of the four divided the chamber, so only one is
-- ingested — see the H.R. 8035 block below.
--
-- Changes NO schema. Additive and idempotent: measures are looked up and RAISE if
-- missing (never find-or-created, so a bare row cannot shadow a curated one), roll
-- calls and member votes and issue rows all ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING. Rolls forward;
-- edits no prior migration. Safe to re-run and safe alongside the runtime ingest.

